course: dictionary
lesson: 7718
title: Publicity: getting noticed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Publicity is the attention that people, events and products get when many people notice them. Newspapers, TV, the internet and the public can all give it. «The rescue got a lot of publicity.» Here it means that lots of people heard about the rescue.
explain: Publicity can also mean the work done to make people notice something, such as adverts, posters and interviews. «The publicity for the film was everywhere.» The film's makers worked hard so that you would see it on posters, on screens and in the news.
explain: Context clues help you. Words like «a lot of» and «everywhere» tell you there was plenty of it. Publicity can be good, when people like what they see, or bad, when people are upset by it. Both are still attention.
fact: Publicity means attention that makes people notice something.
fact: Good publicity makes people think well of something, and bad publicity makes people think badly of it.
fact: A publicity stunt is a surprising act done to get attention.
fact: Publicity can come from newspapers, TV, the internet and the public.
fact: Context clues such as «a lot» and «everywhere» show there was plenty of publicity.
exercise: «The rescue got a lot of publicity.» What does publicity mean here? | A kind of rescue boat | *Attention from newspapers, TV and the public | A map of the sea | Money given to the rescue team
exercise: «The publicity for the film was everywhere.» What kind of thing is publicity in this sentence? | The cinema seats | A very long film | *Adverts, posters and interviews | The popcorn sold at the front desk
exercise: Which of these is an example of bad publicity? | A teacher gives out a prize | A poster shows a new puppy | *A news story says a company cheated its customers | A news story praises a kind bakery
test: «The team staged a stunt to get publicity.» What is a publicity stunt? | *A surprising act done to get attention | A boring meeting about money | A quiet walk in the park | A kind of sweet
test: Mia says publicity is always good. Is she right? | No, publicity only happens on the TV | Yes, because publicity is always money | *No, publicity can be good or bad | Yes, publicity is always good
exam: «Celebrity feuds may be real, exaggerated or even staged for publicity.» What does staged for publicity suggest? | Happened by accident with no one watching | *Arranged to get attention | Cancelled suddenly after a storm | Proved in a court of law
